Third-party code and attributions
================================

FlashInfer/b12x RoCE proxy
-------------------------
helios/native/roce_proxy.c was contributed by its original author from:
https://github.com/local-inference-lab/flashinfer/blob/f5f5341d711f8210ce91af5731a0841570f70e53/flashinfer/experimental/b12x/comm/roce/_roce_proxy.c
The proxy is compiled into Linux aarch64 builds. Its implementation is unchanged
from that revision; Flare adds a license and provenance preamble.
The upstream Apache-2.0 license is reproduced in helios/licenses/FlashInfer.txt
in the source tree and licenses/FlashInfer.txt in binary distributions.

libibverbs
----------
The RoCE proxy uses libibverbs and its inline header interfaces under the
OpenIB.org BSD license alternative. The verbs.h copyright and license notice
is retained in helios/licenses/libibverbs.txt in the source tree and
licenses/libibverbs.txt in binary distributions. The shared library itself
is supplied by the user's operating system.

vLLM
----
Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

ignition/components/markov_sampling.py adapts the sequential vocabulary-block
schedule from vLLM's DS41 fused Markov sampler:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/df3bd094/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/amd/ops/fused_markov.py
Flare's implementation changes score rounding, explicit proposal probabilities,
and random-number domains for its probability-based rejection contract.
The upstream copyright notice is retained in that source file.

ignition/components/four_six_quantization.py adapts the four-or-six NVFP4
quantizer; ignition/components/situ_experts.py adapts SiTU activation,
MXFP8 scale rounding, and SM120 expert arithmetic; ignition/recipes/inkling2/loop.py
adapts the low-rank message controller. Sources are from vLLM PR #69028
(https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/69028), revision b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0/vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/ops/nvfp4.py
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0/vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/ops/activation.py
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0/vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/ops/mxfp8.py
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0/vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/ops/moe_sm120.py
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b3c0ff75424ea9393ce2dbfd2e912bb19f7323f0/vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/loop.py
Flare uses Blackwell hardware E2M1 conversion and binds persistent buffers and
projections for prepared graph execution. The upstream copyright notices are
retained in the adapted files.

hyperflare_recipes/components/megamoe_kernel/inputs.py retains vLLM v0.32.0's
Apache-2.0 Triton input-staging kernel (license text in
hyperflare_recipes/components/megamoe_kernel/LICENSE.vllm), with a wrapper that
selects MXFP8 and validates its buffers without importing vLLM.

DeepGEMM (optional SM103 MegaMoE preparation dependency)
--------------------------------------------------------
The SM103 MegaMoE preparation components in
hyperflare_recipes/components/megamoe*.py and
hyperflare_recipes/components/delivered_fp8_projection.py invoke an externally
installed DeepGEMM fork (https://github.com/local-inference-lab/DeepGEMM, MIT
license with tiered MegaMoE extensions) during preparation. Exported CUDA graphs
retain the compiled kernels; the native serving runtime has no Python or
DeepGEMM dependency.

DS41 SM103 fused decode attention kernels
-----------------------------------------
hyperflare_recipes/components/mega_attention_kernel/include/ carries unchanged
MIT-licensed ds41 W1 attention headers from chronarion/dsv41 commit
f8cd311caf3328ed6f4bb158a7c12811e32a06f8 (sourced from Garner McCloud's
dgx-station-recipes, deepseek-v4.1-flash recipe, commit 8043a68), and
hyperflare_recipes/components/mega_attention_kernel/csrc/w1_attn.cu carries the
upstream launcher with a thread-safe set_num_sms/get_num_sms override of
num_sms() for CUDA Green Context cooperative launch clamping. The upstream MIT
license and attribution notices are retained in
hyperflare_recipes/components/mega_attention_kernel/LICENSE.ds41,
hyperflare_recipes/components/mega_attention_kernel/NOTICE, and
hyperflare_recipes/components/mega_attention_kernel/NOTICE.upstream.

PyTorch
-------
helios/src/frontend/images/resize.rs adapts the resize coefficient generator
and uint8 antialiased convolution from PyTorch's UpSampleKernel.cpp:
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/cf30153c4c131c8164ee7798e5022d810682e2cb/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/UpSampleKernel.cpp
The scalar Rust implementation preserves adaptive coefficient precision and
intermediate uint8 rounding.

PyTorch's copyright notices and BSD-style license terms are reproduced in
helios/licenses/PyTorch.txt and heliopause/licenses/PyTorch.txt in the source
tree, and licenses/PyTorch.txt in the installed Flare package documentation.
The original copyright notices are also retained in the adapted source file.

